\paragraph{NLI validation methodology.}
The NLI gate validation (\S\ref{sec:nli_validation}) uses Qwen3-32B as annotator rather than human judges.
While precision is high (98.9\%), the same model family (Qwen3) serves as both rewriter and validator, introducing potential evaluator-producer bias.
An independent spot-check with GPT-4o is planned to strengthen external validity.

\paragraph{Scale granularity.}
Whether finer-grained scales (1--100 or continuous) could mitigate the Blindspot remains an open question.
Our ordinal regression result ($p = 0.769$) rules out interval-scale assumptions as the cause, but does not exclude granularity effects.

